ATS-301 / review item 3 (WBS XML escaping) -- the escaping is real and needed
========================================================================

THE DEFECT
  tools/update_wbs_ats301.py wrote its note into <x:v> VERBATIM. A note that
  contains '<', '>' or '&' -- a hex digest in angle brackets, a comparison
  operator, an ampersand -- therefore went RAW into xl/worksheets/sheet2.xml,
  which makes the workbook unparseable: Excel refuses to open it and every
  reader of the sheet fails.

THE FIX
  xml_escape() in tools/update_wbs_ats301.py escapes &, < and > BEFORE the text
  goes into the cell. The escape set is the XML spec's own, so the round trip
  through the reader is lossless.

--- PROOF 1: with the escaping, a note containing <24hex> keeps the workbook valid ---
command: python tools/update_wbs_ats301.py
exit code: 0
workbook parses : YES (all XML parts parse)
raw '<a1b2' in sheet2.xml : False   (must be False)
escaped '&lt;a1b2' present: True   (must be True)

  -> the digest text is present, ESCAPED, and the workbook still parses.

--- PROOF 2: WITHOUT the escaping the same note corrupts the workbook ---
command: python tools/update_wbs_ats301.py   (xml_escape() bypassed)
exit code: 0
workbook parses : NO (xl/worksheets/sheet2.xml: not well-formed (invalid token): line 1, column 45419)

  -> WITHOUT the escaping the workbook is CORRUPT. The fix is load-bearing,
     not cosmetic. (The updater itself still exits 0 -- which is exactly why
     this needed an explicit parse check rather than an exit-code check.)

--- restore ---
command: python tools/update_wbs_ats301.py   (restored)
exit code: 0
workbook parses : YES (all XML parts parse)

  -> restored tree: the updater applies cleanly, the workbook parses.

